From: 1q9lugp <lackowork84@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:19:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/29] v3d: no MSAA for 32-bit float colour on 3.3

4x MSAA renderbuffers of R32F, RG32F and RGBA32F came out of a resolve
blit as near-zero data with garbage along the edges (GLES3
fbo.msaa.4_samples.{r32f,rg32f,rgba32f}). Broadcom's driver doesn't
offer them: libGLES_nexus's glxx_max_ms_mode_for_internalformat returns
0 samples for GL_RGBA32F, GL_RGB32F, GL_RG32F and GL_R32F and 4 for
every other format. Report the same, so GL_SAMPLES for these formats
is empty and the cases are NotSupported.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3d_screen.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3d_screen.c b/src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3d_screen.c
index c7e509d..eccdbd7 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3d_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3d_screen.c
@@ -580,6 +580,22 @@ v3d_screen_is_format_supported(struct pipe_screen *pscreen,
         if (sample_count > 1 && sample_count != V3D_MAX_SAMPLES)
                 return false;
 
+        /* 4x MSAA of 32-bit float colour doesn't render on 3.3; Broadcom's
+         * driver gives these formats no samples either.
+         */
+        if (sample_count > 1 && screen->devinfo.ver < 40) {
+                switch (format) {
+                case PIPE_FORMAT_R32_FLOAT:
+                case PIPE_FORMAT_R32G32_FLOAT:
+                case PIPE_FORMAT_R32G32B32_FLOAT:
+                case PIPE_FORMAT_R32G32B32X32_FLOAT:
+                case PIPE_FORMAT_R32G32B32A32_FLOAT:
+                        return false;
+                default:
+                        break;
+                }
+        }
+
         if (target >= PIPE_MAX_TEXTURE_TYPES) {
                 return false;
         }
